<SiteLayout current="training" title="Training Systems — Kimi K3 from Scratch" description="Data, optimizer recipe, GPU performance, reproducibility, and the qualification path to a 6B-token training run.">
  <section class="page-intro"><div class="page-kicker">03 / TRAINING SYSTEMS</div><h1>Making it <em>trainable.</em></h1><p>Implementing a model is only half the work. The training system turns it into a repeatable experiment: bounded data, selected optimizer settings, reliable GPU execution, measurable performance and safe continuation.</p></section>
  <section class="content-section"><div class="section-rail"><span class="section-index">01 / THE PIPELINE</span><span class="rail-line"></span></div><div class="section-main"><div class="section-topline">ENGINEERING THE RUN</div><h2>From corpus to <em>checkpoint.</em></h2><div class="process-grid">
    <div class="process-card"><span>01 / DATA</span><h3>Prepare the corpus</h3><p>FineWeb-Edu sampling, a pinned SmolLM2 tokenizer, deterministic splits and memory-mapped token shards.</p><a class="small-link" href="/docs/data/">Data reference ↗</a></div>
    <div class="process-card"><span>02 / OPTIMIZATION</span><h3>Select the recipe</h3><p>Muon for hidden matrices, AdamW for auxiliary parameters, BF16 autocast, clipping, warmup and cosine decay.</p><a class="small-link" href="/docs/training/">Training reference ↗</a></div>
    <div class="process-card"><span>03 / PERFORMANCE</span><h3>Qualify the GPU</h3><p>Benchmark the real model, measure throughput and memory, and choose changes based on controlled comparisons.</p><a class="small-link" href="https://github.com/adriaflores/kimi-k3-from-scratch/tree/main/experiments/m6">Qualification evidence ↗</a></div>
    <div class="process-card"><span>04 / RELIABILITY</span><h3>Resume safely</h3><p>Save optimizer state, loader cursors, RNG and counters, and verify backups before extending the run.</p><a class="small-link" href="/docs/reproducibility/">Reproducibility ↗</a></div>
  </div></div></section>
  <section class="content-section"><div class="section-rail"><span class="section-index">02 / THE RECIPE</span><span class="rail-line"></span></div><div class="section-main"><div class="section-topline">PRETRAINING CONTRACT</div><h2>A carefully bounded <em>experiment.</em></h2><p class="section-lead">The 6B-token configuration follows preliminary training studies, target-GPU qualification and a completed 80M-token pilot. The final run continues from the pilot state rather than restarting.</p>
    <div class="spec-grid"><div><strong>H100 NVL</strong><span>Target GPU</span></div><div><strong>BF16</strong><span>Compute precision</span></div><div><strong>32 × 1,024</strong><span>Tokens / update</span></div><div><strong>Muon + AdamW</strong><span>Hybrid optimizer</span></div><div><strong>3 × 10⁻³</strong><span>Peak learning rate</span></div><div><strong>6B</strong><span>Token horizon</span></div></div>
    <p class="notice">The full training horizon and final model-quality evaluation are separate claims. The site reports the pilot as validated, and reserves final model-quality evidence for Results.</p>
